  "id": "neutral-point",
  "term": "neutral point",
  "definition": "In this context, a neutral point is the position on a facial emotion continuum where a person judges a face as equally happy and angry. It marks the perceiver’s balance point for seeing an expression as neither leaning clearly positive nor clearly negative.",
